Vendored tools — bundled into the macOS app alongside scripts/.

exiftool   Perl script + lib/ from Image-ExifTool distribution (exiftool.org).
           Currently v13.50. To update: download a new tar.gz, replace
           exiftool and lib/.

tag        macOS Finder tag CLI (github.com/jdberry/tag), MIT licensed.
           Source vendored at tag-src/. Build on macOS:
             scripts/tools/build-tag.sh
           Or copy from Homebrew:
             cp $(brew --prefix)/bin/tag scripts/tools/tag
           The built binary is gitignored — each developer builds locally.

gyroflow   Gyroflow (gyroflow.xyz), used for .gyroflow project generation.
           Not vendored here: the CLI inside Gyroflow.app only runs from inside
           that bundle, so the whole app is installed alongside Jetlag rather
           than copied into it:
             scripts/tools/download-gyroflow.sh
           It reports an existing install (/Applications/Gyroflow.app, the
           Application Support tools directory, or $PATH) instead of
           downloading, and otherwise installs Gyroflow.app into
           ~/Library/Application Support/Jetlag/tools/. Pass --check to report
           presence without downloading.
